


STIME(2)            UNIX Programmer's Manual             STIME(2)



NAME
     stime - set time

SYNOPSIS
     stime(tp)
     long *tp;

DESCRIPTION
     _S_t_i_m_e sets the system's idea of the time and date.  Time,
     pointed to by _t_p, is measured in seconds from 0000 GMT Jan
     1, 1970.  Only the super-user may use this call.

SEE ALSO
     date(1), time(2), ctime(3)

DIAGNOSTICS
     Zero is returned if the time was set; -1 if user is not the
     super-user.

ASSEMBLER (PDP-11)
     (stime = 25.)
     (time in r0-r1)
     sys stime





























